          "text": "{\n  \"target_identification\": {\n    \"speaker\": \"Pierre\",\n    \"addressee\": \"Hélène\",\n    \"anchor_quote\": \"Je vous aime!\"\n  },\n  \"target_translation\": \"I love you.\",\n  \"dimensions\": {\n    \"T\": {\n      \"score\": 4,\n      \"evidence_status\": \"assessable\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.98,\n      \"reason\": \"The expression directly presents Pierre's love for Hélène as true. His immediately preceding private thought uses the same proposition, although the awkward, formulaic delivery leaves his sincerity and the nature of the feeling complicated.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"block_id\": \"target\",\n          \"quotation\": \"Je vous aime\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"block_id\": \"scene\",\n          \"quotation\": \"«Теперь уж поздно, всё кончено; да и я люблю ее», подумал Пьер.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"P\": {\n      \"score\": 2,\n      \"evidence_status\": \"assessable\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.82,\n      \"reason\": \"The focal words occur within the social ratification of an engagement: Hélène is already described as Pierre's fiancée, and Pierre recalls that this is what one says on such occasions. Thus the declaration moderately affirms and invokes his accepted position as her fiancé and the associated undertaking to marry her. It is not itself an explicit proposal or a newly specified promise; Prince Vasily's blessing is a separate speech act that supplies the ceremonial context.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"block_id\": \"scene\",\n          \"quotation\": \"Пьер молча держал руку своей невесты\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"block_id\": \"scene\",\n          \"quotation\": \"— Je vous aime! — сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях; но слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"block_id\": \"scene\",\n          \"quotation\": \"— Друг мой Леля! Я очень, очень рад. — Голос его задрожал. — Я любил твоего отца... и она будет тебе хорошая жена... Бог да благословит вас!...\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"E\": {\n      \"score\": 0,\n      \"evidence_status\": \"assessable\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.95,\n      \"reason\": \"The utterance is not represented as a reflexive or spontaneous discharge of affect. Pierre deliberately searches for the conventional words appropriate to the occasion and is embarrassed by their inadequate sound.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"block_id\": \"scene\",\n          \"quotation\": \"«Что-то такое особенное говорят в этих случаях», думал он, но никак не мог вспомнить, чтó такое именно говорят в этих случаях.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"block_id\": \"scene\",\n          \"quotation\": \"слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"O\": {\n      \"score\": 0,\n      \"evidence_status\": \"assessable\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.9,\n      \"reason\": \"No substantial residual force requires a separate category. The direct avowal is covered by T, while its conventional role in affirming the engagement is covered by P.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"block_id\": \"target\",\n          \"quotation\": \"Je vous aime\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"block_id\": \"scene\",\n          \"quotation\": \"вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"original_speech_situation\": \"After the assembled family has treated Pierre and Hélène as engaged and Prince Vasily has blessed them as a future married couple, they are left alone. Following Hélène's kiss, Pierre recalls the expected formula for the occasion and tells her, awkwardly, that he loves her.\",\n  \"affection_evidence\": \"mixed\",\n  \"undertaking_and_uptake\": \"The expression moderately affirms Pierre's socially established role as Hélène's fiancé and thereby invokes the undertaking to marry her; it does not state detailed terms or independently formulate a proposal. Hélène has already kissed him and is described as his fiancée, so the bond is treated as mutually and socially accepted. The supplied passage later reports that they marry, but Pierre's hesitation, shame, sense of inevitability, and formulaic delivery leave the voluntariness and emotional basis of his commitment uncertain.\",\n  \"recognised_work\": true,\n  \"recognition_note\": \"The supplied passage is recognisable as Leo Tolstoy's War and Peace.\",\n  \"limitations\": \"The passage supports the avowal and its engagement context but does not conclusively settle the depth or durability of Pierre's affection. The classification relies only on the supplied scene and does not infer omitted circumstances.\"\n}"
